## Context
`.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` has a `changes` job (dorny/paths-filter@v3,
`predicate-quantifier: every`, single brace-glob `chore` filter). Its comment
claims: "chore is true ONLY when *every* changed file matches the chore filter …
Fail-safe: ambiguity always builds." The observed behaviour is the opposite.

## Observation (evidence, 2026-06-10)
- PR #938 — files `slides/manuscript/main.md` + `tickets/closed/0523-….erg` →
  filter `chore = true` → **all** build steps skipped (report, slides,
  manuscript, make check). The CI run shows every build step `skipped`.
- PR #939 — files `slides/Makefile` only → `chore = false` → build ran.

So a **mixed diff containing any** `tickets/`/`.claude/`/`docs/`/STATE/README
file skips the **entire** docs-build — including `report.pdf` and `slides.pdf`,
the real deliverables — even when the same diff also changes source or the
manuscript. This is how #938's `main.md` change merged without CI building
anything.

## Cause — not yet isolated
Hypothesis: `predicate-quantifier: every` over a **single** pattern is a no-op,
so the filter reduces to "true if any changed file matches the chore globs",
which is the inverse of the intent. VERIFY against dorny/paths-filter semantics
(docs or a minimal test) before changing the config — do not fix on the
hypothesis alone.

## Relevant files
- `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` — `changes` job, lines ~16–28

## Test (write first)
Two synthetic diffs exercised against the filter logic:
- chore-only diff (e.g. a `tickets/**` file alone) → build steps SKIP.
- mixed diff (a `tickets/**` file + a `slides/**` or `src/**` file) → build
  steps RUN. (Currently this case wrongly skips.)

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A diff with at least one non-chore file always runs the full docs-build.
- [ ] A purely-chore diff still skips (the optimisation is preserved).
- [ ] The workflow comment matches the actual behaviour.
